     "quote": "Platelets or thrombocytes (from Ancient Greek  θρόμβος (thrómbos) 'clot' and  κύτος (kútos) 'cell') are a part of blood whose function (along with the coagulation factors) is to react to bleeding from blood vessel injury by clumping to form a blood clot.",
